            <ArticleTitle>Wanted: Effective Followers in Surgery.</ArticleTitle>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1097/SLA.0000000000002510</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="BRIEF DESCRIPTION" NlmCategory="METHODS">This SURGICAL PERSPECTIVE paper brings to our readers the general topic of &quot;followership.&quot; Leadership has received a lot of attention in the administrative education domain; however, there is a history of academic research on the role and importance of the effective follower. We review some of the critical articles in this field, and present a possible approach for incorporating the notion of effective followership in a surgical context.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
